# Gitignored files to copy into every worktree Claude Code creates.
#
# .gitignore syntax. Only a file that BOTH matches a pattern here AND is
# gitignored is copied, so nothing tracked is ever duplicated.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#
# A worktree is a fresh checkout, so an untracked file simply is not in it. That
# is structurally the 136550a defect: `SCIAGENT_TABLE_CACHE` was set in an
# untracked `.claude/settings.local.json`, no worktree checkout could contain it,
# and every worktree silently took the 3m11s cold-cache path against 1.055s warm
# (docs/DECISIONS.md, 2026-08-16). The cache lookup itself is now resolved from
# `git rev-parse --git-common-dir` and needs no variable, but the file still
# carries machine-local permissions and any future env, and the failure mode --
# a setting that is simply absent, silently -- is the one worth closing.
#
# Belt and braces rather than strictly necessary: since v2.1.211 a permission
# approval granted in a worktree is saved to the main checkout's
# settings.local.json and applies everywhere. That statement is about where
# *approvals* are written, not about how an `env` block in that file resolves,
# so this stays.
.claude/settings.local.json
